Documentation for mul
---------------------
rev 0.3, 2/5/99:  Added support for HalfHeight layout
rev 0.4, 2/10/99:  Corrected to support all flavors of {unsigned,signed}x{unsigned,signed}:
                   replaced SignExtendInputs with A={Signed,Unsigned,Both} and 
                   B={Signed,Unsigned,Both}
rev 0.5, 2/19/99:  Changed from TSMC25 icons to MMI generic icons
rev 0.6, 2/22/99:  Added support for NBITS_A != NBITS_B and NBITS_B != power of 2
rev 0.7, 3/9/99:   Updated to final versions of MMI generic icons
                   Added support for NBITS_A != power of 2
rev 0.8, 4/30/99:  No changes to mul.sue, just to underlying generators	
rev 0.9, 5/11/99:  No changes to mul.sue; Changed base cell names to MMIG_


The multiplier generator is used to derive a multiplier made up of 4:2 adder
trees.

The complete multiplier is made up of these three generators:  
  ppg:  partial product generation logic
  mul_array:  multipler array made up of 4:2 adders
  adder:  carry propagate adder, forms the final result

ppg and adder can be optionally included or excluded, to allow for substitution
of different types of logic, or insertion of pipe latches.

GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NBITS_A:
    Definition:
      The number of bits in input value A_H.  The width of the
      multiplier's output will be NBITS_A + NBITS_B.
    Legal Values:
      4, 8, 16, 32, 64
    Default:
      8

  NBITS_B:
    Definition:
      The number of bits in input value B_H.  The width of the
      multiplier's output will be NBITS_A + NBITS_B.
    Legal Values:
      4, 8, 16, 32, 64 (note: must be the same value as NBITS_A)
    Default:
      8

  UseMulCin:
    Definition:
      This argument makes the multiplier's carry in bits accessible to 
      the user, or not.  If the user elects not to use the carry ins,
      they will be wired to a logic 0.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" and "N".
    Default:
      Y

  AddExtraCSA:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify that an extra row of carry 
      save (4:2) adders be included in the multiplier array.  In addition,
      two extra input vectors (CSA_A_H and CSA_B_H), each of width NBITS_A 
      + NBITS_B, are provided as the additional inputs to this final row of 
      adders.
      This feature allows the user to implement a multiply-adder, or multiply-
      accumulator.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" and "N".
    Default:
      N

  IncludePPG:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify whether the partial product
      generation logic is included in the multiplier.  If IncludePPG = Y,
      the ppg generator is used to generate simple (nand-invert) ppg logic.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" and "N".
    Default:
      Y

  A:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify whether the multiplier's A
      (multiplier) input is signed or unsigned.  The user can choose Signed,
      Unsigned, or Both.  If Signed is chosen, the generated multiplier will
      always treat the A input as a signed number.  If Unsigned is chosen, the
      generated multiplier will always treat the A input as an unsigned number.
      If Both is chosen, logic is included to allow the A input to be treated
      as either signed or unsigned, based on the ASigned_H control signal.
      NOTE:  there are area and speed consequences to these choices.  Unsigned
        is the smallest and fastest.  Signed is very slightly larger and slower.
        Both is noticeably larger and SIGNIFICANTLY slower, and requires the use
        of the ASigned_H control signal which drives across the width of the 
        multiplier.  It is highly recommended that you choose with care.
      NOTE:  Sign extension etc. is performed only in the PPG logic, so if
        IncludePPG = N, the value of A is ignored.
      NOTE:  If Signed or Both is chosen, the msb of MCin_L is used in order
        to correctly perform a multiplication of a negative value of A.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Signed", "Unsigned", and "Both".
    Default:
      Unsigned
      
  B:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify whether the multiplier's B
      (multiplicand) input is signed or unsigned.  The user can choose Signed,
      Unsigned, or Both.  If Signed is chosen, the generated multiplier will
      always treat the B input as a signed number.  If Unsigned is chosen, the
      generated multiplier will always treat the B input as an unsigned number.
      If Both is chosen, logic is included to allow the B input to be treated
      as either signed or unsigned, based on the BSigned_H control signal.
      NOTE:  there are area and speed consequences to these choices.  Unsigned
        is the smallest and fastest.  Signed is very slightly larger and slower.
        Both is noticeably larger and SIGNIFICANTLY slower, and requires the use
        of the BSigned_H control signal which drives across the width of the 
        multiplier.  It is highly recommended that you choose with care.
      NOTE:  Sign extension etc. is performed only in the PPG logic, so if
        IncludePPG = N, the value of B is ignored.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Signed", "Unsigned", and "Both".
    Default:
      Unsigned
      
  IncludeCPA:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify whether the carry propagate
      adder which forms the multiplier's final result is included in the
      generated schematics or not.  Omitting the carry propagate adder 
      allows the user to generate their own special purpose adder, or 
      insert registers at the multiplier tree's output.
      If the adder is included, a carry select adder of width NBITS_A +
      NBITS_B is inserted at the output of the multiplier tree.  This adder 
      is generated from the adder generator.  The adder's carry in and carry
      out signals are accessible to the user.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" (include carry propagate
      adder) and "N" (omit adder).
    Default:
      Y

  HalfHeight:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify that the layout be done in
      (NBITS_A + NBITS_B)/2 bit positions, instead of (NBITS_A + NBITS_B) 
      bit positions.  Note that if (NBITS_A + NBITS_B)/2 is an odd number of
      bit positions, the layout will actually fit in 
      ((NBITS_A + NBITS_B)/2 + 1) bit positions.
      This configuration results in a slightly slower and less area 
      efficient design.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" (half height layout)
      "N" (full height layout).
    Default:
      N

  bitslice:    
    Definition:
      This argument directs DPC to enforce bitslice layout, or not.  
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" and "N".
    Default:
      Y


INPUT SIGNALS:
--------------
If IncludePPG = Y:
  A_H (multiplier) and B_H (multiplicand)
If IncludePPG = N:
  PP*_H (partial product vectors)
If AddExtraCSA = Y:
  CSA_A_H, CSA_B_H (extra inputs to the final row of CSA's)
If UseMulCin = Y:
  MCin_L, MCarry_H (carry in values to multiplier array)
If IncludeCPA = Y:
  ACin_H (adder carry in)
If A = Both:
  ASigned_H
If B = Both:
  BSigned_H


OUTPUT SIGNALS:
---------------
If IncludeCPA = Y:
  Result_H (final multiply result)
  ACout_H (adder carry out)
If IncludeCPA = N:
  Sum_H, Carry_H (multiply array redundant outputs)


